\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\title{Transit Timing Variations in Compact Exoplanet Systems}
\author{A. Volkov and S. Reyes}
\date{January 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Timing Model}
The mid-transit time of orbit number $n$ follows a linear ephemeris:
\begin{align}
t_n &= t_0 + n P
\end{align*}
Deviations from this line reveal gravitational perturbations from companion planets,
and the amplitude of the deviation encodes the mass of the perturber.
\end{document}

